          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.083,
            0.883,
            0.122
          ],
          "content": "(v) When we heat camphor in one corner of a room, the fragrance reaches all corners of the room."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.123,
            0.882,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": "(vi) On heating, we are adding energy to the camphor, and the energy is released as a smell."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.162,
            0.883,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": "3. Choose the correct answer with justification. If we could remove all the constituent particles from a chair, what would happen?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.302,
            0.22,
            0.543,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": "(i) Nothing will change."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.295,
            0.238,
            0.78,
            0.257
          ],
          "content": "(ii) The chair will weigh less due to lost particles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.257,
            0.661,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Nothing of the chair will remain."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.277,
            0.739,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": "4. Why do gases mix easily, while solids do not?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.298,
            0.883,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": "5. When spilled on the table, milk in a glass tumbler, flows and spreads out, but the glass tumbler stays in the same shape. Justify this statement."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.356,
            0.883,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": "6. Represent diagrammatically the changes in the arrangement of particles as ice melts and transforms into water vapour."
